- audit evidence deliberately excludes names, emails, phones, addresses, request payloads and autonomous `REQUIRES_NEW` audit writes;
- audit rows are historical operational evidence and are not an analytics warehouse.

OH-016 must preserve that distinction. Analytics may consume a stable application contract or purpose-built projection, but it must not directly query `workforce` persistence tables or import workforce persistence classes.

## Module ownership

Introduce a first-class `analytics` Spring Modulith module.

- operational modules remain source of truth for business state and operational evidence;
- `workforce` continues to own Staff/workforce operational and audit state;
- `authorization` continues to own authorization decisions and permission vocabulary;
- `analytics` owns analytical subject identity/pseudonymization where required, analytical fact schemas, data classification, retention metadata/policy and derived analytical projections introduced by this slice;
- analytics facts are not mutable replacements for operational truth;
- analytics must not become a backdoor authorization source.

Cross-module references use explicit application/named contracts and opaque identifiers. Analytics must not depend on foreign persistence entities, foreign JDBC repositories or direct SQL against another module's schema.

## Core invariants

### Purpose-bound analytical facts

- every persisted analytical fact has an explicit bounded fact type/schema and schema version;
- free-form request/response payloads are not analytical fact storage;
- fact attributes are limited to information required by a documented analytical purpose;
- Tenant scope is explicit on every Tenant-derived fact;
- timestamps distinguish when the business fact occurred from later analytical processing time where both are needed;
- correlation identifiers may be retained when necessary for traceability but must not become high-cardinality metric labels;
- analytical facts do not mutate operational state.

### Subject privacy / pseudonymization

- analytical facts must not use raw JWT subjects, external identity-provider identifiers, email, phone, address or display name as subject identity;
- when a subject must be correlated across facts, use an analytics-owned opaque/pseudonymous/internal analytical subject key rather than copying operational PII into fact rows;
- any reversible source-to-analytical-subject mapping, if required, is separated from analytical fact tables and treated as more sensitive than the fact stream itself;
- subject resolution must be Tenant-consistent and deterministic/stable only to the extent required by the analytical purpose;
- deletion/unlink semantics for identifying mappings must not corrupt unrelated operational source-of-truth records.

The exact pseudonymization implementation is decided in ADR-0014 from the minimum concrete requirements; do not introduce encryption/KMS/tokenization infrastructure without a proven need.

### Data classification and retention

- analytical data classes are explicit and bounded rather than arbitrary strings;
- each persisted fact class has an explicit retention policy or an explicit documented reason for retained-until-deletion semantics;
- retention belongs to analytics and must not delete immutable operational audit evidence owned by another module;
- expired analytical facts must be removable through a tested repository/application boundary when the selected retention policy requires deletion;
- retention cleanup must be Tenant-safe and concurrency-safe for the chosen persistence design;
- the design must allow later legal/business retention changes without rewriting historical migrations.

### Derived projections

- analytical projections/scores are derived artifacts, not mutable truth on StaffProfile/User/CustomerProfile;
- a projection is versioned or otherwise tied to an explicit calculation definition;
- no employee ranking, automated performance score, disciplinary signal or consumer profile is introduced in this slice;
- OH-016 establishes the boundary required for later analysis but does not silently turn workforce audit facts into employee-performance evaluation.

### First concrete producer: workforce operational evidence

- use an already-existing OH-014 workforce fact/evidence path as the first executable analytical source;
- expose only the smallest stable workforce application/named contract required for analytics;
- analytics must not query `workforce.audit_events` directly;
- the initial analytical projection must remove direct operational identity when that identity is not required by the analytical purpose;
- bounded workforce facts such as action/outcome and organizational-state transitions may be represented when justified;
- raw free-form reason text or PII must not be introduced merely because analytics persistence exists;
- failure to project/persist analytics must not falsify whether the original workforce operation committed. The selected consistency semantics must be explicitly documented and tested rather than hidden behind an autonomous transaction.

ADR-0014 must decide whether the first analytics ingestion is synchronous composition, durable pull/projection, Spring Modulith application event, or another minimal mechanism based on actual failure/recovery requirements. Do not introduce a broker or transactional outbox by default.

