- `OperationalFact` / typed analytical fact contract or equivalent;
- bounded `FactType` and schema-version semantics;
- explicit analytical data classification;
- analytics-owned subject key / subject-resolution boundary where correlation is required;
- retention policy/value object and expiration calculation;
- analytical fact repository with explicit Tenant isolation;
- purge/retention application boundary when retention requires deletion;
- one concrete workforce-to-analytics projection path;
- separation between identifying subject mapping and privacy-reduced analytical facts if a mapping is required;
- observability that uses bounded fact type/outcome dimensions only.

Names are not fixed by this issue; ADR-0014 must justify the smallest coherent model.

## Persistence / consistency direction

- PostgreSQL remains the only database technology for this slice;
- V1-V16 remain byte-identical;
- while OH-015 is in flight, OH-016 must not use V17-V20; any OH-016 migration starts at V21 or later;
- analytics owns its own schema/tables if persistence is justified by ADR-0014;
- analytics persistence must not create foreign keys into mutable workforce/customer/order rows merely for convenience;
- cross-module historical identity remains via opaque contracts/identifiers;
- structural invariants that belong in PostgreSQL must have PostgreSQL constraint tests;
- no JVM-local lock is a correctness boundary;
- no Redis, broker, warehouse, lake, graph database, vector database or separate analytics service is introduced without measured evidence.

